### 📤 PHASE 6 — Exports (Excel + PDF) (45 min)

**Goal:** Buttons on client detail page that export to Excel and PDF.

**Steps:**
- 6.1 `npm install exceljs jspdf jspdf-autotable`
- 6.2 Prompt Cursor:
  > "Create `app/api/clients/[clientId]/export/excel/route.ts` that:
  > 1. Verifies auth + audit logs the export
  > 2. Fetches the client's P&L, transactions, and budget data from BigQuery
  > 3. Generates an Excel file with 3 sheets: Summary, Transactions, Budget vs Actual
  > 4. Uses ExcelJS, applies basic formatting (bold headers, currency format)
  > 5. Returns the file as a download
  > Then add an 'Export to Excel' button on the client detail page that hits this endpoint."
- 6.3 Prompt Cursor:
  > "Create `app/api/clients/[clientId]/export/pdf/route.ts` that:
  > 1. Verifies auth + audit logs the export
  > 2. Generates a clean PDF with: client name + month, key metrics (revenue, profit, runway), transactions table
  > 3. Uses jsPDF + jspdf-autotable
  > 4. Returns the file as a download
  > Add a 'Export to PDF' button."
- 6.4 Test:
  - Open client detail → Excel download → opens cleanly.
  - PDF download → opens cleanly.
  - Audit log in admin panel shows both export actions.
- Commit:
  ```bash
  git add .
  git commit -m "Phase 6: Excel and PDF exports working"
  ```

---

### 🛡️ PHASE 7 — Security hardening (30 min)

**Goal:** Production-grade security without overengineering.

**Steps:**
- 7.1 Prompt Cursor:
  > "Add basic rate limiting to all API routes:
  > 1. Create `lib/rate-limit.ts` using `@upstash/ratelimit` (or a simple in-memory limiter for now)
  > 2. 60 requests per minute per user
  > 3. Returns 429 if exceeded
  > 4. Apply to /api/clients, /api/clients-overview, /api/clients/[clientId], and all admin routes
  > Explain why rate limiting matters."
- 7.2 Confirm every sensitive action writes to AuditLog:
  - Viewing client data
  - Exports
  - Inviting members
  - Changing roles
  Ask Cursor to scan the codebase for missing audit logs.
- 7.3 Prompt Cursor:
  > "Add Zod validation to all POST/PUT API routes:
  > 1. Define a schema for each endpoint's expected body
  > 2. Validate before processing
  > 3. Return 400 with a useful error if validation fails
  > Show me one example, then add it to all routes."
- 7.4 Prompt Cursor:
  > "Add security headers to next.config.js:
  > - Content-Security-Policy
  > - X-Frame-Options: DENY
  > - X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  > - Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  > - Permissions-Policy
  > Explain what each header prevents."
- 7.5 Final security checklist (must all pass):
  - [ ] `.env.local` is gitignored
  - [ ] No API keys outside `.env.local`
  - [ ] Every API route checks auth FIRST
  - [ ] Admin routes check role
  - [ ] BigQuery service account has ONLY Data Viewer + Job User
  - [ ] Rate limiting on all routes
  - [ ] Zod validates all POST bodies
  - [ ] Security headers in next.config.js
  - [ ] HTTPS enforced (Vercel default)
- Commit:
  ```bash
  git add .
  git commit -m "Phase 7: Security hardening complete"
  ```

---

### 🚀 PHASE 8 — Deploy to Vercel (30 min)

**Goal:** Live URL like `onform-internal-tool.vercel.app` to share with Henry.

**Steps:**
- 8.1 Push to GitHub:
  ```bash
  gh repo create onform-internal-tool --private --source=. --remote=origin --push
  ```
  Or manually: new repo on github.com (private, no README) → then:
  ```bash
  git remote add origin https://github.com/<user>/onform-internal-tool.git
  git branch -M main
  git push -u origin main
  ```
- 8.2 Vercel → **+ Add New → Project** → import the repo → don't change defaults.
  Add EVERY env var from `.env.local`:
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`
  - `CLERK_SECRET_KEY`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL` = `/sign-in`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL` = `/sign-up`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_IN_URL` = `/dashboard`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_UP_URL` = `/dashboard`
  - `CLERK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`
  - `DATABASE_URL`
  - `GOOGLE_PROJECT_ID`
  - `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS_JSON`
  - `DATA_STUDIO_DASHBOARD_URL`
  - `RESEND_API_KEY` (when Resend is set up)
  Click **Deploy** → wait ~2 min → get URL.
- 8.3 Update Clerk:
  - Clerk dashboard → app → **Domains** → add Vercel URL.
  - Re-add webhook with new URL: `https://<vercel-url>/api/webhooks/clerk`.
  - Copy new webhook secret → Vercel env vars → redeploy.
- 8.4 Test in production: fresh sign-up → dashboard loads → exports work → admin panel works.

**Debug rule:** if it works locally but fails on Vercel, **check env vars first** (Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables).

---

### 🎓 PHASE 9 — Teaching pass (recommended, don't skip)

**Goal:** Cement the learning. This is where engineering instincts form.

**Steps:**
- 9.1 `git checkout -b learning`
- 9.2 Delete a key file you don't fully understand.
- 9.3 Prompt Cursor:
  > "I deleted [filename]. Don't write it back yet. Instead, walk me through what this file should contain, step by step. After each section, ask me to write it myself, then check my work. We're learning."
- Repeat for:
  - `middleware.ts`
  - `app/api/clients/route.ts`
  - `lib/bigquery.ts`
  - `lib/prisma.ts`
- After each file, prompt:
  > "Now quiz me with 5 questions about how this file works. After my answers, tell me what I got right and wrong."
- 9.4 Add a small extra feature (favourites toggle, search bar, last-login display). Prompt Cursor:
  > "I want to add [feature]. Don't write the code. Ask me how I think we should structure it, then guide me through writing it myself."

---

## 7. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES — RUNNING LIST

All belong in `.env.local` (dev) and Vercel env vars (prod). Never in code.

```env
# Clerk
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=/sign-in
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL=/sign-up
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_IN_URL=/dashboard
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_UP_URL=/dashboard
CLERK_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# Database (Railway)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:...

# Google Cloud / BigQuery
GOOGLE_PROJECT_ID=onform-data-warehouse
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS_JSON='{"type":"service_account",...}'  # one line, single-quoted

# Data Studio
DATA_STUDIO_DASHBOARD_URL=https://lookerstudio.google.com/...

# Resend (email)
RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
```

**Rules:**
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` is exposed to the browser. Anything else is server-only.
- Restart `npm run dev` after editing `.env.local` (env loads on start).

---

## 8. GLOSSARY

| Term | Plain English |
|---|---|
| Component | Reusable piece of UI (button, card, form) |
| Hook | React function for state/effects (`useState`, `useEffect`) |
| Route | A URL path in the app (`/dashboard`) |
| API route | A URL that returns JSON, not HTML |
| Server component | Runs on the server, ships HTML only |
| Client component | Runs in the browser; needs `'use client'` at top |
| Middleware | Code that runs before any route — often for auth |
| Webhook | An external service calling back when something happens |
| Environment variable | Secret value stored outside the codebase |
| Singleton | One shared instance across the app |
| ORM | Library that turns SQL into TypeScript |
| Migration | Versioned change to the database schema |
| CORS | Browser security around cross-domain requests |
| JWT | Signed token used for auth |
| Service account | Credentials for the app (not a person) to access Google services |

---

## 9. TROUBLESHOOTING (when things break)

**"Module not found":**
- `npm install` again, restart dev server.

**"Unauthorized":**
- Check `.env.local` has all keys. Restart dev server (env loads on start).

**BigQuery empty / errors:**
- Check service account has correct roles.
- Validate JSON env var: `node -e "console.log(JSON.parse(process.env.GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS_JSON))"`.

**Vercel deploy fails:**
- Read the build log — error is usually specific.
- 90% of failures: env variable missing or typo.

**Clerk webhook not firing locally:**
- `ngrok http 3000` → temporarily point Clerk webhook at the ngrok URL.

**General "I don't understand":**
- Paste error + relevant code into Cursor: "What does this error mean? Walk me through it."
- Fallback: Stack Overflow / Next.js Discord.

